WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:10.750
Should you preemptively kill a zombie? Of
course! I believe it was either Pliny

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:15.820
the Elder or Ving Rhames who said,  "It is
good to kill zombies". But on this matter,

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.349
I suspect the founders would consult
John Locke. Stipulated, there are many

00:00:20.349 --> 00:00:25.899
kinds of zombies: fast, slow, undead, rage
virus, Chicago voters. But in every case,

00:00:25.899 --> 00:00:30.250
the societal collapse of a zombie
apocalypse qualifies as what John Locke

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.030
called a "state of war", a state of
permanent conflict of all against all

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:37.030
like in "The Walking Dead" or a Black
Friday sale at Target.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:42.100
All the zombies want to eat your face or
brains. For Locke, this is "a settled

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:47.590
design upon another man's life." Locke
continues "one may destroy a man who

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:52.960
makes war upon him... for the same reason
he may kill a wolf or lion... because such

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.880
men are not under the ties of the commonlaw
of reason, and... will be sure to

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:03.399
destroy him whenever he falls into their
power." Well, if humans need killing in that

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.620
context, surely there's no need to debate
the undead.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.260
How will you prepare for the zombie apocalypse?

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.350
Let us know in your
comments! Also, let us know what other

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:19.360
topics you'd like our scholars to cover
in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:25.110
subscribe for more research and videos
from AEI.

